window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>It’s Halloween in Whisper Cove. To Harper Harlow-Monroe that means candy, parties, and costumes to celebrate her favorite holiday of the year. That’s what she’s expecting anyway. What she gets is the exact opposite.<br> <br> When her husband Detective Jared Monroe calls to tell her there’s a ghost on County Line Bridge throwing items at passing cars and causing accidents, Harper is hoping for a quick takedown but that’s not what she gets.<br> <br> The ghost isn’t just hanging out on the bridge because she’s bored. No, Whisper Cove’s former librarian is protecting a body.<br> <br> Nobody knows how the teenager got there. Even his parents are confused. All anybody knows is that the librarian died in her sleep in the past…and yet she’s protecting the boy’s body in the present.<br> <br> As Harper digs deep she starts uncovering some troubling stories about the boy’s friends and what might have happened to the librarian. How does it all fit together, though?<br> <br> Harper won’t give up until she knows the truth. What if the truth is more than anybody can bear?</p>"; 
